new tent city is opened on the greek  island of lesbos this facility is meant  to  house migrants left homeless after fire  destroyed the notorious  moria refugee camp but most of those  displayed say conditions on lesbos are  so unbearable that they want to leave  for mainland europe  greece's prime minister is calling on  other european union countries  to help out and take in more migrants  new arrivals settle into life in the  replacement migrant camp on lesbos  while the facility is still being built  greek authorities remain  hopeful all will be re-housed within the  week  since the notoriously overcrowded moria  camp burned down  most migrants have been forced to sleep  on the streets  iraqi refugee and photographer yusuf  ashwali  is angry at just how desperate  conditions have become  look at the people sleeping  in the gas stations on the streets and  the roads  no masks no medical care  here is the children  [Music]  look at the children  look at the children  some migrants have even chosen to stay  at the scorched moria camp  locals say they too are angry at the  situation  we are approaching disaster there is no  growth  we should have tourism but we have had  nothing for five years now we are living  in a constant state of fear  five hundred migrants became one  thousand and two thousand  and we are still in the same situation  this is a disgrace the authorities  fooled us  they must leave as soon as possible we  treated them well when they first came  but they destroyed our island the greek  government is also to blame  most migrants on lesbos just want to  leave the island  but they fear the new camp means that  won't be happening  anytime soon
 

